# AI Agent Model Lanes

This project uses LiteLLM as the client-facing gateway for local and provider
model lanes. Cursor agents should use the lane names and role boundaries below
instead of talking directly to individual vLLM runtimes.

Gateway:

```text
http://litellm.hom.lab/v1
```

Profile contract:

```text
/Users/joshc/develop/dotfile-vnext/.cursor/ai-agent-profiles.json
```

## Rules

- Use `litellm.hom.lab` as the gateway surface when a custom OpenAI-compatible
  base URL is available.
- Do not point Cursor directly at `vllm-runtime`, localhost, or one-off node
  ports for normal project work.
- Preserve the user-approved model lane set. Do not collapse work to
  `deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B-GGUF` just because it is the first runtime path.
- Treat model catalog entries with `pending_research` or `provisional_example`
  status as not selected for download or pinning.
- Include trace metadata in tool/client wrappers when available:
  `agent_role`, `model_lane`, `routing_policy`, `context_class`.

## Agent Roles

- `planner`: default lane `ripi-private`, alternate lane
  `code-fast`, boundary `read_only`,
  context `private_planning`
- `coder`: default lane `deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B-GGUF`, alternate lane
  `code-fast`, boundary `repo_write`,
  context `implementation`
- `tester`: default lane `code-test`, alternate lane
  `code-fast`, boundary `test_execution`,
  context `validation`
- `reviewer`: default lane `code-review`, alternate lane
  `ripi-private`, boundary `read_only`,
  context `review`
- `documenter`: default lane `code-fast`, alternate lane
  `deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B-GGUF`, boundary `repo_write`,
  context `documentation`
- `steward`: default lane `ripi-private`, alternate lane
  `code-review`, boundary `governance`,
  context `planning_governance`

## Model Lanes

- `deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B-GGUF`: architecture, refactors, hard coding; status `pending_research`; example `Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-AWQ`
- `experiment`: smoke tests and trial models; status `provisional_example`; example `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`
- `code-fast`: autocomplete, small edits, repo questions; status `selected`; backend HVH-01 Ollama `qwen2.5-coder:1.5b` via LiteLLM (same as `code-autocomplete-1.5b`)
- `code-review`: critique, risk finding, test review; status `pending_research`; family `reviewer/risk-finding model`
- `code-test`: test generation and focused test repair; status `pending_research`; family `test generation/repair model`
- `ripi-private`: private planning, governance, and conversation; status `pending_research`; family `private local reasoning/planning model`
- `embeddings-local`: local retrieval and index embeddings; status `pending_research`; family `embedding model`
- `public-research`: public docs, comparison, and research; status `deferred`; family `cloud/provider route unless local model is selected`
